1462	    // col-block; packed-GQA (rep>1, rep|CM) uses one 3D [64,rep,CM/rep] box per col-block (mapQ is built
1463	    // accordingly by the launcher). Both land in the same swizzled tile gather_row_k would have built, so
1464	    // the per-item Q reload is one async TMA (not a 128-row cp.async gather) -- which is what makes the
1465	    // persistent ring WIN for GQA/MQA (the gather reload serialized and lost to the per-tile grid).
1466	    // Paged / rep-not-dividing-CM keep the cp.async gather.
1467	    // Q is NEVER paged (only K/V) -> Q can use TMA even when K/V uses the cp.async COOP gather (USE_TMA=0).
1468	    // TMA_Q decouples this (FA3: Use_TMA_Q independent of Use_TMA_KV): the paged persist launches TMA_Q=1
1469	    // so the per-work-item Q reload is ONE async TMA box (cheap) instead of the 128-lane cp.async gather --
1470	    // the reason the paged persist previously lost to the per-tile grid.
1471	    const bool tmaq     = TMA_Q && (rep == 1);
1472	    const bool tmaq_gqa = TMA_Q && (rep > 1) && (CM % rep == 0);
